Logical operators AND, OR, NOT are used in condition checking. Like a AND b checks if both a and b are true.
a OR b checks if either of a or b is true. !a complements the boolean value of a.


class Solution {
    String booleanOperations(boolean a, boolean b) {
        return (a && b) + " " + (a || b) + " " + (!a);
    }
}
